src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v33.json:2: "_note": "Version 33 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v32 answers): entries identical to version 32; role-v33 names a customer's, supplier's, competitor's or partner's reported figure beside its action as kind (2), with two examples (a customer's order backlog; a supplier's gross margin on higher prices), as the standard's kind 2 example does (a customer's quarterly revenue, growth and backlog); v32 dropped a memory supplier's reported results, the model reading the subject line as limiting evidence to the company (its own account). Version 32 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v31 answers): entries identical to version 31; role-v32 narrows 'a research or award result' to 'a published paper or an award'; in v31 the model read a competitor developing its own chip as an unscaled research result (its own account, page on the competitor's chip report). Version 31 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v30 answers): entries identical to version 30; role-v31 narrows v30's rejection to an integration of the company's software, models or tools into others' products or research, or a research or award result, without business scale, and names a customer's purchase, order or deployment and a choice of supplier or rival as actions; v30's wording (adoption, partnership, a hospital chain running the vendor's software) dropped a bank choosing a rival's chips, a cloud's deployment of the company's systems and the company's choice of a supplier's CPU. Version 30 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v29 answers): entries identical to version 29; role-v30 rejects an adoption, integration, partnership or research result that gives no business scale even when well-known names take part (standard section 2: product details without business scale); v29 kept about 55 such records on the 37 articles whose reference keeps nothing. Version 29 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v28 answers): entries identical to version 28; role-v29 names the company's own leases besi